# Next.js migration (أثَر)

Flask remains the **data plane** (`/api/*`, fonts, audio, editor). Next.js in `frontend/` is the **public product UI**. Do not re-implement Quran logic in Next; call Flask via `/backend-api/*`.

## Public Next doors (done)

| Path | Door | Notes |
|---|---|-----|
| `/` | landing | Four doors + credits footer |
| `/read` | المصحف | Study drawer includes iʿrāb; Flask `/read` still has older chrome |
| `/memorize` | تثبيت | Viewport studio: mushaf fills remaining height. Range, reciter, repetition, and transport stay on-screen. التفصيل الموضوعي is off by default and lives under الموضع. ASR stays Flask |
| `/waqf` | مُكْث | Scrollable verse-first study: search, word-flow + inspector, breath plan, full matrix, all-reciters gallery, classical-for-all. Lab stays Flask |
| `/waqf-practice` | تدريب | Tap words + grade vs printed marks. ASR + live tajweed stay Flask |
| `/credits` | المصادر | Attribution page |
| `/robots.txt` `/sitemap.xml` `/llms.txt` | SEO | Next copies of Flask SEO |

## Stay on Flask (intentional — do not port in a UI pass)

- **API + fonts + audio proxy** — Vercel must not proxy long audio/CV/PDFs
- **`/waqf-lab`** — research workspace (Quran-wide search, reciter matrix, classical-for-all)
- **ASR** — zipformer on `/memorize` and `/waqf-practice` (132MB+)
- **Editor** (`ENABLE_EDITOR`): `/mushaf-editor`, `/layout-studio`, `/azhar-layout`, `/font-lab`, `/cv-waqf`, `/waqf-mark-review`, `/classical-review`, `/activity`, quran-integrity-review

## Known gaps (next passes, not forgotten)

- تثبيت: tajweed color on studio; التفصيل الموضوعي parked under الموضع
- تدريب: printed mushaf page-card layout (tap-to-grade currently uses word flow)
- Reader: leftover Flask-only chrome via `HandoffSurface`

When adding a public door, wire **nav**, **landing**, **in-app handoffs**, and `smoke.spec.ts`. Keep Quran wording/tafsir from local APIs or Tafsir/Bahouth MCP — never invent.
